00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:10,879
For this, we're going to take the response messages.

143
00:09:10,879 --> 00:09:13,840
So this is the trajectory that we have above.

144
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,120
And then we're going to add in some feedback.

145
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:20,480
This can be in a few different formats, but the simplest format is just a string.

146
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:27,600
So here we're going to take in this feedback, always sign your emails, John Doe.

147
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:33,560
We now need to define the prompts that we want to potentially update.

148
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:36,840
Each entry in this list should have four keys.

149
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:39,160
First is the name of the prompt.

150
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:41,760
Next is the value of the prompt.

151
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,200
Next is update instructions.

152
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:46,080
These are instructions for how you should update the prompt.

153
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:49,360
And then finally, we have the when to update key.

154
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,240
These are instructions for when you should update the prompt.

155
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:56,880
So under the hood what's going to happen is we're first going to use the when to update

156
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:00,680
value to determine which prompts if any to update.

157
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:05,080
If we determine that it's worth updating, we're then going to use the update instructions

158
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:10,560
and apply that to the original prompt to get a new updated prompt.

159
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:14,800
Here we filled these in for the four prompts that we want to potentially update.

160
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:19,080
So we have the main agent prompt which we're going to get the most current values from

161
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:22,680
this agent instructions key.

162
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,200
The update instructions are just going to be keep the instruction short into the point

163
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,880
and we're actually going to use that for all of them.

164
00:10:28,879 --> 00:10:32,600
And then when to update, update this prompt whenever there's feedback on how the agent

165
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:36,639
should write emails or schedule events.

166
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:38,919
What about triage ignore?

167
00:10:38,919 --> 00:10:40,759
Similarly we're going to name it that.

168
00:10:40,759 --> 00:10:44,159
We're going to fetch the most recent value from long-term memory, updating instructions

169
00:10:44,159 --> 00:10:48,519
are the same, and then update this prompt whenever there's feedback on which emails should

170
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:50,519
be ignored.

171
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:55,519
Triage notify and triage respond are pretty similar except rather than updating it when

172
00:10:55,519 --> 00:10:58,080
there is information about when the emails should be ignored.

173
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:01,639
We're going to update it when there's information about when the user should be notified

174
00:11:01,639 --> 00:11:04,000
or responded.

175
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,560
After we do this, we're going to create the multi-promped optimizer.

176
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:11,759
We're going to use Anthropics Cloud3Sonic model to optimize the prompt.

177
00:11:11,759 --> 00:11:17,000
We've found that it's currently the best for this type of prompt optimization.

178
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,759
Kind equals prompt memory is the algorithm that we're going to use to update the prompt.

179
00:11:21,759 --> 00:11:26,520
This is the simplest one and you should look at the API reference of Langmem for more complicated

180
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:28,600
examples.

181
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:35,240
This optimizer itself is a graph, so we're going to invoke it by passing in these trajectories

182
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:40,519
and then these prompts, and we're going to get back this updated variable.

183
00:11:40,519 --> 00:11:43,600
Let's take a look at what this returns.

184
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:48,039
We can see that it returns a list of prompts.

185
00:11:48,039 --> 00:11:53,079
These have all the same keys as before, so the name prompt update instructions and went

186
00:11:53,079 --> 00:11:54,079
to update.

187
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:59,040
Now some of these prompts may be different than before, and we can actually see that

188
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:04,120
here, the first main agent prompt, it's prompt is now different.

189
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:07,120
When sending emails, always sign them as John Doe.

190
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:10,320
This is the feedback that we passed in.

191
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:15,400
Once we have these updated prompts, we can loop through them and update the long-term

